<instruction name="BSWAP">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Byte Swap</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261266">
   <string>Reverses the byte order of a 32-bit or 64-bit (destination) register. This instruction is provided for converting little-endian values to big-endian format and vice versa. To swap bytes in a word value (16-bit register), use the XCHG instruction. When the BSWAP instruction references a 16&#8209;bit register, the result is undefined.</string></para>
  <para unique="1261267">
   <string>In 64-bit mode, the instruction&#8217;s default operation size is 32 bits. Using a REX prefix in the form of REX.B permits access to additional registers (R8-R15). Using a REX prefix in the form of REX.W promotes operation to 64 bits. See the summary chart at the beginning of this section for encoding data and limits.</string></para>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261268"><string>IA-32 Architecture Legacy Compatibility</string></title>
   <para unique="1261269">
    <string>The BSWAP instruction is not supported on IA-32 processors earlier than the Intel486&#8482; processor family. For compatibility with this instruction, software should include functionally equivalent code for execution on Intel processors earlier than the Intel486 processor family.</string></para>
   </section>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1261287">
   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Exceptions (All Operating Modes)">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#UD </string></term>
    <listitem><string>If the LOCK prefix is used.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
